diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..48cd76b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+# Orders & Payments service
+
+A small FastAPI service for placing orders, taking payments and issuing refunds. Data lives in a
+single SQLite file; payments and email go through thin HTTP client wrappers.
+
+## Layout
+
+| Path | What lives there |
+| --- | --- |
+| `app/main.py` | App factory; includes every router and initialises the database on start-up. |
+| `app/routes/` | HTTP handlers: orders, payments, refunds, users, inventory, exports, webhooks. |
+| `app/services/` | Business logic: pricing, order lifecycle (`order_state`), inventory, invoices. |
+| `app/clients/` | Wrappers for the payment gateway and the email API. |
+| `app/auth.py`, `app/idempotency.py`, `app/db.py` | Sessions, idempotency keys, SQLite access. |
+| `tests/` | Offline tests; the gateway and email clients are swapped for `httpx.MockTransport`. |
+| `REVIEW.md` | The team's review rules (R1-R9) for this service. |
+
+## Running it
+
+```
+uvicorn app.main:app
+```
+
+Tables are created on start-up if they are missing. Any ASGI server works; `app.main:app` is the
+entry point.
+
+## Configuration
+
+All configuration comes from environment variables (see `app/settings.py`):
+
+| Variable | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `DATABASE_PATH` | `orders.db` | SQLite file. |
+| `EXPORT_DIR` | `exports` | Where `GET /exports/orders` writes its files. |
+| `TAX_RATE` | `0.0825` | Tax rate applied to the discounted subtotal. |
+| `HTTP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | `5` | Timeout for gateway and email calls. |
+| `SESSION_TTL_SECONDS` | `86400` | How long a login session lasts. |
+| `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_URL`, `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_API_KEY` | example URL, empty | Payment gateway. |
+| `EMAIL_API_URL`, `EMAIL_API_KEY` | example URL, empty | Transactional email. |
+| `WEBHOOK_SECRET` | empty | Shared secret for signing webhook bodies. |
+
+## Money
+
+Amounts are `Decimal` dollars everywhere in the service and are rounded half up to whole cents by
+`models.to_money`. Floats are rejected. Amounts are stored as text in SQLite and sent to the
+gateway as strings.
+
+## Order lifecycle
+
+Order status changes only through `order_state.transition()`, which enforces these moves:
+
+```
+pending   -> paid, cancelled
+paid      -> shipped, refunded, cancelled
+shipped   -> delivered, refunded
+delivered -> refunded
+```
+
+`cancelled` and `refunded` are final.
+
+## Money-moving endpoints
+
+`POST /payments/capture` and `POST /refunds` require an `Idempotency-Key` header. Repeating a
+request with the same key and body returns the saved response; reusing the key for a different
+request, or while the first request is still running, returns 409.
+
+## Tests
+
+```
+python -m pytest
+```
+
+Run from this directory. Each test gets a fresh SQLite file in a temporary directory.
